# Archives and raw bags never belong in the repository: GitHub rejects
# any single file over 100 MB, and a bag or a zip of bags cannot be
# diffed or partially fetched, so it burdens every clone forever.
# Convert bags with analysis/freeflight_pack.py and commit the packed
# arrays instead (measured 97x on case_01/Mx); archive the originals
# externally and cite the DOI in the Data Availability statement.
# These patterns only guard new files -- the excitation bags already
# tracked under DataSet/exp are unaffected.
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.7z
*.bag
*.db3

# cached traces for analysis/ge_dynamics_figure.py (regenerable, ~MBs)
analysis/.ge_dynamics_traces.npz

# cached estimator results for analysis/mff_table.py (regenerable)
analysis/mff_table.pkl

# cached collection pass for analysis/residual_budget.py (regenerable)
DataSet/exp/residual_budget_cache.pkl
